EXTENSION "ArM5_Hedge_Magic_Runes" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Hedge Magic [Revised Edition] - Runes"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-07-26"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Hedge_Magic_Core_Ext"

    #tt3oWoQSU435qugp6sY51dsy ^"Ansuz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "A" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Mouth" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "communication, teaching"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Freya’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "This rune has many meanings, including \"mouth\" as in the source of speech and also the beginning of a river. It originated as \"god,\" as it is associated with the Norse gods who are called the Aesir (\"AYS-eyr\"), and particularly symbolizes Odin, the father of the gods, who first discovered the power of the runes.\n\nWhen used to describe a target, Ansuz most commonly refers to images, specifically sounds. For the purposes of Penetration, this application is an Imaginem effect. Ansuz can also affect the mind through speech, an aspect of Mentem, and in rare circumstances it can target the human mouth directly as a Corpus effect. It is also occasionally associated with Vim, to target intelligent supernatural beings that have the power of speech.\n\nFor as long as the runes last, the target may hear the words spoken by spirits and incorporeal beings and can tell the difference between illusory noises and real noises as if he had a score of this effect's magnitude in Second Sight. The runes are usually drawn upon an amulet made of wood or stone and worn against the person's skin, and thus typically last only a short while.\n\nAnsuz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of the effect to all Ability rolls associated with Communication.\nGeneral: The target gains the power to recognize audible illusions of less than or equal to the level of this effect, recognizing them by ear much in the same way those with Second Sight perceive them visually.\nLevel 10: Give a target the ability to speak. If the target is not intelligent, it can only repeat what is specified in the effect.\nLevel 20: The target gains the power to recognize the Form associated with the Might of any creature within about ten paces. This tells the vitki which runes can be used to target it.\nLevel 25: The target gains the ability to intuitively understand the surface thoughts of others within a ten-pace area, making it possible to make sense of foreign languages.\nLevel 30: Increase or decrease a target's Communication by one point, to no more than the average score for a being of that type. Each additional magnitude increases the number of points or the upper limit, but never more than 5 above or below the average score."
            REFERENCES {
                "Second Sight" -> #t2Lm60x9JehOADnxby9Oub7N ^"Second Sight"
                "Second Sight" -> #t2Lm60x9JehOADnxby9Oub7N ^"Second Sight"
            }
        }

        #t4LiQ0Tb0LfWZy6vBLDngMPe ^"Berkanan" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "B" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Birch" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "health, youth"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Tyr’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "The birch is a tree of fertility; its branches are bare and do not produce flowers or seeds, but it sprouts many shoots and leaves. In Norse legend, Odin marked the runes on nine birch twigs and then struck an adder with them, so that it was killed and divided into nine parts.\n\nThe Berkanan rune is associated with healing, and also with youth. When used as a target it is usually Herbam, though it can also affect children (Corpus), and young animals (Animal).\n\nBerkanan Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty to recovery rolls equal to (the magnitude of the effect x 3). This includes physical injuries, but not sickness from diseases or poisons.\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty to all Ability rolls performed while injured.\nLevel 15: The target will not impregnate or become pregnant for the duration. Ensure that the target is potent or fertile for the duration.\nLevel 20: Heal one of the target's Light Wounds or the equivalent, or reduce one of a target's wounds by one level of severity (changing a Heavy Wound to a Medium Wound, for example).\nLevel 20: Prevent all of a target's Light Wounds from healing naturally for the duration.\nLevel 25: Heal your target's Medium Wound, or reduce a wound by two levels of severity.\nLevel 25: Prevent all of a target's Light or Medium Wounds from healing naturally for the duration.\nLevel 30: Heal a target's Heavy Wound, or reduce one of a target's wounds by three levels of severity.\nLevel 30: Prevent all of a target's Light, Medium or Heavy Wounds from healing naturally for the duration.\nLevel 35: Heal a target's Incapacitating Wound.\nLevel 35: Prevent any of a target's wounds from healing naturally for the duration of the spell.\nLevel 40: Heal all of the target's wounds."
        }

        #tlNfIuBSWOfCjIfjG9Jc2eEH ^"Dagaz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "D" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Day" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "time, growth"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Tyr’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Dagaz means \"day,\" as in the length of time it takes the sun to travel from horizon to horizon. Thus, the rune is associated with the concept of time. It also represents the sun, light, and life during long, cold winters. Things grow over time, and so Dagaz is also associated with the growth of animals, plants, and people.\n\nAs a target, Dagaz would be considered part of either Imaginem or Ignem, specifically affecting the light of day and moving images associated with time passing, but it is rarely used in this way.\n\nDagaz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to Ability rolls that involve a regular, day-long activity.\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty to Aging rolls equal to the magnitude of the effect, so long as the rune lasts for the entire year.\nLevel 20: Cause a target to grow twice its normal size with the passing of the sun.\nLevel 20: Shrink a target to half its normal size with the passing of the sun.\nLevel 30: Cause a target to grow to full maturity in a single day.\nLevel 30: Age target five years, as long as the target has already reached maturity."
        }

        #ts2C1nIm4RD4nsSUyxtmudzw ^"Ehwaz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "E" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Horse" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "speed, relationships"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Tyr’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "This rune stands for the horse — a beast noted for its stamina, speed, and strength. It represents superior mobility in combat, as well as the close relationship between horse and rider. When used as a target, it is associated with Animal, specifically when targeting horses or other animals used in battle.\n\nEhwaz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of the effect on all rolls performed while mounted, including Initiative, Attack, and Defense rolls.\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of the effect on Ability rolls involving Quickness (not including Initiative or Defense).\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of the effect to all rolls that involve trust and loyalty between two individuals, creating a bond similar to that of horse and rider. This is similar to the effects of the True Friend Virtue.\nLevel 20: Tame the target, making it more loyal and sensitive to the vitki's needs.\nLevel 30: Summon a mount, which obeys the vitki's instructions and accepts him as a rider.\nLevel 30: Increase or decrease a target's Quickness by one point, to no more than the average score for a being of that type. Each additional magnitude increases the number of points or the upper limit, but never more than 5 above or below the average score."
        }

        #tkzeMjW9fAWY8xTrjcngH3nB ^"Fehu" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "F" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Wealth" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "wealth, domesticated animals"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Freya’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Fehu is the rune of wealth, represented by good fortune and prosperity. In contrast to Othila, which is associated with things such as land and heirlooms, Fehu is typically thought of as common wealth — things like cattle and other animals, silver pennies or surplus grain — but not tools, clothing, or weapons. In the Norwegian and Icelandic rune poems, wealth is more cynically viewed as a \"source of discord among kinsmen\" perhaps in reference to the brutal nature of Viking raids.\n\nWhen used as a target, Fehu is usually associated with either Animal or Terram, depending upon the type of wealth affected by the rune. It can be used to affect animals in general, but only those that are domesticated and thus considered property.\n\nFehu Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to Ability rolls that support the target gaining wealth: working, gambling, investing, or treasure-hunting.\nLevel 20: The target gains the ability to detect precious metal he is within about ten paces.\nLevel 25: The target gains the ability to detect domesticated animals within about ten paces.\nLevel 35: Summon wealth, usually in the form of precious metal or a domesticated animal."
        }

        #tCLvy15Sb1sHveW1YsqQA81l ^"Gebo" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "G" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Gift" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "debt, sacrifice"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Freya’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Accepting a gift places the recipient under certain obligations in Norse society, which usually involves the need to return the favor with another gift of similar value, so that neither party is in the other's debt. Thus, while this rune does represent openhanded charity and generosity, it also represents an arrangement or promise that binds the recipient.\n\nGebo is not associated with any particular Form, but with any physical object given as a gift. It can also be used to target someone in the vitkir's debt, through that sense of obligation created by the vitkir's generosity. In this case, it might be considered a Mentem effect.\n\nGebo Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect on all Ability rolls to influence others, including forming new relationships, courtship, charming others, and negotiation.\nLevel 30: Give the target a feeling of deference and obligation to the vitki.\nLevel 35: Force the target to obey a simple command.\nLevel 40: Force the target to obey a complex command.\nLevel 50: Completely dominate the target's mind and emotions."
        }

        #tFqamnDpn44wGxlij3ENPrZT ^"Hagalaz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "H" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Hail" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "weather, illness"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Heimdall’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Hagalaz represents the cruelest side of nature, from sudden storms to debilitating illness. It means hail, both in terms of weather and a hail of missiles. It is associated with great destruction and harm, and always brings pain and suffering to its target. In the rune poems it is called \"the whitest of grain, whirled from the vault of the heavens and tossed about by wind before finally turning to water.\" It is a powerful force that is difficult to control.\n\nWhen used as a target, Hagalaz is almost always part of Auram or specific aspects of Aquam (cold, rain, and hail). It can also affect other sorts of missile weapons, including Terram (stones) and Herbam (arrows).\n\nHagalaz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to Damage.\nGeneral: Cause hail or other dangerous phenomena to pummel a target, inflicting damage equal to a stress die + (the Level of the effect – 15).\nLevel 15: Summon severe weather phenomena, like thunderstorms or hailstorms.\nLevel 20: Cause weather phenomena to become more or less severe.\nLevel 25: Summon a very severe weather phenomenon; for example, a tornado or a blizzard."
        }

        #t46l4sqhp2LDKVny6XDsqwS5 ^"Isa" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "I" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Ice" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "cold, stasis"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Heimdall’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Isa means ice, and it symbolizes the hidden dangers ice represents, such as slipping or breaking. It embodies coldness, and also cold emotions. As a target, Isa is associated with literal ice (Aquam), or Ignem when affecting temperature, or Mentem when affecting a person's cold and implacable feelings.\n\nIsa Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty that's equal to the magnitude of this effect to Ability rolls that involve ice or the cold: exposure, winter travel, or slipping.\nGeneral: Chill a target, doing Damage equal to (the level of the effect – 20) and potentially freezing it solid.\nLevel 10: Cause water to freeze. If cast on a target, this makes it cold to the touch; living beings lose a Fatigue level. Cause ice to melt.\nLevel 15: Cause a target to feel depressed and apathetic for the duration, canceling out other strong emotions.\nLevel 20: Hold a target totally motionless.\nLevel 25: Cause the surface of a target to become completely covered in ice."
        }

        #tlkL0pRjn2RW8oZmME7yhExp ^"Jera" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "J" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Year" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "harvest, bounty"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Heimdall’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Jera signifies the harvest, and while this implies autumn it can also mean the bounty of nature all year round. The harvest is also the end result of hard work for an entire year, and so the rune also has connotations of prosperity and plenty. As a target, Jera is almost always associated with the form of Herbam, though it can also influence an Animal harvest, and can target people's health and general well being through Corpus.\n\nJera Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to year-long activities, so long as the rune lasts for the entire year, with the bonus gained at the end of the year. For example: harvest, study, teaching, craft work (but not aging, which is covered by Dagaz).\nGeneral: Target is immune to supernatural diseases of up to this effect's Level.\nLevel 5: Ensure that the target remains healthy and strong, immune to natural blight and illness for the duration.\nLevel 15: Summon food and drink."
        }

        #t6uBZtZamwZ6iKBHTY6lkx5E ^"Kauno" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "K" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Pain" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "fire, sores"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Freya’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "In the Anglo-Saxon Rune Poem, Kauno is described as a torch visible from afar, while other rune poems refer to it as an abscess or boil. As a pale, bright flame it could also refer to a fever, which \"burns where princes sit within.\" Thus, the rune symbolizes heat, the color and light of flames, and burning pain.\n\nAs a target, Kauno affects any kind of fire, as well as heat and temperature. It is almost always associated with Ignem when evaluating Penetration, though effects that cause sores and pain are usually Corpus or Animal.\n\nKauno Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to this effect's magnitude to all Ability rolls associated with disease and sickness, such as diagnosing or curing others.\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty to all Ability rolls performed while sick.\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty to recovery rolls due to sickness and disease equal to (this effect's magnitude x 3). This does not include recovery rolls for physical injuries.\nLevel 10: Ignite an extremely flammable target, or cause it to become warm to the touch. This does +5 Damage to the target or anything touching it each round, with the Damage total divided by 5 after rolling.\nLevel 15: Ignite a very flammable target, or cause it to become hot to the touch. This does +5 Damage to the target or anything that's touching it each round, with the Damage total divided by 2 after rolling.\nLevel 20: Ignite a flammable target, or cause it to become hot enough to boil water. This does +5 Damage to the target or anything touching it each round.\nLevel 20: Cause the target to suffer from painful sores that last for the duration. These are distracting and unpleasant for the target, but have no other effect.\nLevel 25: Ignite a slightly flammable target, or cause it to become hot enough to glow. This does +10 Damage to the target or anything touching it each round.\nLevel 25: The target is infected with a minor illness, which will not heal naturally for the duration.\nLevel 30: Ignite a barely flammable target, or cause it to become hot enough to melt lead. It does +15 Damage to the target or anything touching it each round.\nLevel 30: The target is infected with a serious illness, which will not heal naturally for the duration.\nLevel 35: Ignite a target, or cause it to become unnaturally hot. This does +20 Damage to the target or anything touching it each round.\nLevel 35: The target is infected with a major illness, which will not heal naturally for the duration.\nLevel 40: Ignite a target, or cause it to become unnaturally hot. This does +25 Damage to the target or anything touching it each round.\nLevel 40: The target is infected with a critical illness, which will not heal naturally for the duration.\nLevel 45: Ignite a target, or cause it to become unnaturally hot. This does +30 Damage to the target or anything touching it each round.\nLevel 45: The target is infected with a terminal illness, which will not heal naturally for the duration."
        }

        #tIR1t1TLr20FUqDP8Qin0rc7 ^"Laguz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "L" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Water" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "ocean, ships"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Tyr’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "This rune represents water, especially of the ocean. There is great wealth and power in the ocean, and many hidden dangers that cannot be seen from the surface. As a target it is almost always associated with Aquam, though it can also affect things that are only found underwater, such as water-breathing animals and sea plants.\n\nLaguz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to Ability rolls performed while submerged in or floating upon water.\nLevel 5: The target gains the ability to see clearly through water.\nLevel 10: Summon water, enough to fill an area about ten paces across and ten paces deep.\nLevel 20: The target gains the ability to sense the direction of the nearest large body of water, or if any water is within about ten paces.\nLevel 20: The target gains the ability to breathe water.\nLevel 25: Speed a sea journey, causing the target ship or the target swimmer to travel through the water at twice the normal speed.\nLevel 30: Cause waves to knock over a large target or to pull a small target under water."
        }

        #tvKAC6pu9t0WY0P4lyDU094r ^"Mannaz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "M" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Man" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "cooperation, duty"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Tyr’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Mannaz means mankind, and suggests unity and cooperation among all people. When used as a target it affects either the mind or the body, but most often the body, and thus is usually linked to Corpus rather than Mentem. It is used most frequently to affect a person as the target of another rune.\n\nMannaz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to Ability rolls that involve Dexterity (but not Attack rolls).\nGeneral: Target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to Ability rolls involving working with others, such as fighting in a group or collaborating on a project in a workshop.\nLevel 20: Inspire feelings of cooperation and unity within a group of targets. Cause a group of fighters to function as a trained group.\nLevel 30: Increase or decrease a target's Dexterity by one point, to no more than the average score for a being of that type. Each additional magnitude increases the number of points or the upper limit, but never more than 5 above or below the average score."
        }

        #tuEHga7i7q87cmDIHUO8lhwL ^"Naudiz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "N" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Need" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "trouble, hardship"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Heimdall’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Naudiz is a very negative rune, meaning hardship, trouble, and adversity, often scratched onto a fingernail to indicate great need. It may be used to target things that are desperate, dying, or despairing, and so is usually associated with Mentem or Corpus.\n\nNaudiz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect when in great need, such as when dreadfully wounded or in a desperate state of emotion.\nGeneral: The target suffers a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect on all Ability rolls that he has tried once and failed.\nGeneral: Delay the resolution of another supernatural effect no greater than the level of this effect, putting it off for as long as this rune lasts, and casting it when this spell is broken. This spell must include the runes for the held effect as well as Naudiz. For example, to delay an Ansuz effect of Level 20, the rune spell must be Naudiz (Ansuz) 20 or less.\nGeneral: Bind an active rune spell of Level less than or equal to this one, so that the duration lasts as long as the runes used in this spell. The spell must include the runes for the bound effect as well as Naudiz. For example, to bind a Fehu (Ansuz) effect of Level 15, the rune spell must be Naudiz (Fehu, Ansuz) 15 or greater.\nLevel 20: Cause a target to feel a deep despair, which makes him unable to use Confidence Points for the duration of the spell."
        }

        #tofpiEilAi57B39CeyKEedYg ^"Ingwaz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "Ng" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Lord" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "family, security"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Tyr’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Ingwaz is associated with peace, family, and a safe, secure home. As a target, it may affect a building, dwelling, or structure, and so is often tied to Herbam and Terram. It can also affect all those who live in a particular house, making it possible to target them by carving runes on the outside, or to target members of the caster's family or household. This is usually a Corpus effect.\n\nIngwaz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to Ability rolls that affect his family, household, or home.\nLevel 20: The target gains an instinctive sense of where his family is, including distance and direction and their current emotional state.\nLevel 20: The target gives birth easily and the baby is healthy, so long as the rune is worn by her for the whole of the pregnancy.\nLevel 35: Summon a target person, transporting him or her to the caster."
        }

        #taKfGYqDqDkkOJ3One5FjkwY ^"Othila" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "O" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Inheritance" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "lands, possessions"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Tyr’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "The Othila rune means property, but specific material goods as opposed to Fehu, which represents general wealth. These are things that can be passed on from generation to generation, such as lands or possessions, and thus the rune is most often used as a target tied to Terram.\n\nOthila Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to all rolls that involve a specific tool or family heirloom, such as wielding his father's sword or defending his lands. This includes Initiative, Attack, and Defense rolls.\nLevel 15: Make an object more effective at what it is designed to do. For example, make a sword light and sharp, or a plow till the earth more quickly. The object functions as if it were exceptional quality, and reduces the number of potential botch dice by two when used.\nLevel 20: Summon a target to the caster; this must be a nonliving thing that is smaller than a person, such as a sword or chest."
        }

    #tMBzwk4Fwqid7yufdPSBOlXi ^"Perth" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "P" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Cup" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "chance, secrets"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Heimdall’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Perth is a mysterious and strange rune, with many different interpretations. Perhaps the strongest association is with fate and chance, though it is also tied to pleasure and relaxation, such as found at a gaming table or dining hall. Thus, it typically represents a container that holds secrets, such as a dice cup or drinking horn. In the Anglo-Saxon Rune Poem it represents a piece on a gaming board, a pawn.\n\nOften Perth is used to affect the supernatural realms, particularly Magic. It is thus tied most strongly to Vim. It can target vis, and it can also target other spells and supernatural effects. It does not affect supernatural beings and creatures with Might (these are Ansuz if they are intelligent, or Uruz if they are not), though it can affect their powers.\n\nPerth Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to rolls that involve pure chance, such as when playing at dice. This also influences events governed by some element of chance, such as shooting an arrow into the dark or determining whether or not a woman becomes pregnant.\nGeneral: Whenever the target rolls for a potential botch, the number of potential botch dice is reduced or increased by the magnitude of this effect.\nGeneral: All supernatural effects cast on the target that are less than or equal to half this effect's level are dispelled.\nLevel 10: The target can sense Magic or Faerie auras within about ten paces, and identify their strength.\nLevel 20: The target gains the ability to sense and identify vis that is within about ten paces.\nLevel 25: The target can recognize the caster of any active magic in the vicinity, or can get a general sense of the effects, much like reading the inscribed description of a rune spell."
        }

        #tseUnmovdAYI6zvWd7I5jLuM ^"Raido" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "R" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Riding" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "travel, knowledge"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Freya’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "This rune is generally held to mean \"riding,\" as in the activity of going forth on horseback or on a cart. The word raido may be related to the Old Norse word reid, which means either chariot or thunder, and thus it may invoke Thor, the Norse god of thunder, who rode in a great chariot. It symbolizes a journey, and all forms of travel. It also conveys the idea of preparation for war or severe weather, and is thus associated with principles of planning, thought, and strategy.\n\nAs a target, Raido targets a cart, ship, or wheel, as well as the tack and harnesses of animals that pull a cart or chariot. The animals themselves are usually associated with either Ehwaz if they are horses, or Fehu for other domesticated animals.\n\nRaido Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect on all Ability rolls made while traveling, such as Area Lore, Folk Ken, Ride, or Charm. This does not include mounted combat.\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect on all natural Ability rolls associated with Stamina (but not Soak or casting rune magic).\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to his Initiative.\nLevel 15: Repair a harness or wheel.\nLevel 20: Restore a lame animal, healing a Light Wound for the duration. The target gains the power to sense which direction it is traveling.\nLevel 30: Speed a journey, allowing the target to run and walk at twice the normal speed.\nLevel 30: Increase or decrease a target's Stamina by 1 point, to no more than the average score for a being of that type. Each additional magnitude increases the number of points or the upper limit, but never more than 5 above or below the average score.\nLevel 35: Summon a target to the caster; it must be a nonliving thing that is larger than the caster, such as a boat or cart."
            REFERENCES {
                "Folk Ken" -> #tiRSLLY6ibe94vbvYQaIeDsb ^"Folk Ken"
            }
        }

        #tmszRoG0ppVWjJgOEsySlYdR ^"Sowilo" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "S" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Sun" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "triumph, virtue"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Heimdall’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Sowilo is associated with light and the sun, and is described as a boon to sailors and a blessing for travelers. It also has overtones of good succeeding against evil, much as light triumphs over dark. As a target Sowilo affects light, and is thus a part of the Form of Ignem. It can also target the Divine and beings that have Divine Might as a subset of Vim.\n\nSowilo Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to natural Ability rolls associated with Perception.\nGeneral: The target can see through illusions of this effect's level or less as if he had Second Sight, including seeing through regiones.\nLevel 10: The target gains the ability to see in the dark as if it were daylight. The target can sense Divine or Infernal auras within about ten paces, and identify their strength.\nLevel 20: Extinguish all light within about ten paces of the target. Make a target invisible.\nLevel 25: The target becomes more resistant to cold, and is immune to the ill effects of exposure.\nLevel 25: Cause blindingly bright sunlight to shine on or from the target.\nLevel 30: Increase or decrease a target's Perception by 1 point, to no more than the average score for a being of that type. Each additional magnitude increases the number of points or the upper limit, but never more than 5 above or below the average score."
            REFERENCES {
                "Second Sight" -> #t2Lm60x9JehOADnxby9Oub7N ^"Second Sight"
            }
        }

        #thXYyIDt0YuEix1WcrGkGufv ^"Tiwaz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "T" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Tyr" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "justice, battle"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Tyr’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Tyr is the Norse god of truth and battle, giver of victory and protector of the other gods. He is loyal to his fellows and known for sacrificing his hand to the Fenris wolf so that it could be bound. His rune is associated with men who fight for the good of their companions, and who seek truth. As a target, it is primarily associated with Mentem and justice, in that it affects a person's thoughts and deeper motivations.\n\nTiwaz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to Personality rolls that involve positive emotions like loyalty or bravery.\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to his Attack or Defense scores.\nGeneral: The target may boost his Confidence Score by 1, as long as his Confidence Score is no greater than (the magnitude of this effect – 3).\nLevel 15: The target gains the ability to sense the direction in which the nearest person is located\nLevel 20: The target gains an intuitive understanding of those people's thoughts and motivations within about ten paces, allowing him to more easily make friends or figure out the social structure of a community.\nLevel 30: The target gains the ability to tell if people within ten paces believe that they are telling the truth or lying.\nLevel 45: The target can completely understand the minds and emotions of those people within about ten paces, and can accurately predict their actions and reactions."
        }

        #tLUmPhf893yupB174eA57gFc ^"Thurisaz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "Th" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Ogre" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "malice, shapeshifting"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Freya’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Thurisaz is interpreted many different ways, usually with a negative connotation. The Norse and Icelandic rune poems describe it as meaning \"giant\" or \"ogre,\" noting that such creatures especially like to harm women, while the Anglo-Saxon poem calls it \"thorn,\" being sharp and severe. The rune is also said to be used to evoke demons from the underworld. Its symbolism is generally evil and dangerous, and because of its association with trolls and ogres it is often used to cast spells that change the caster's shape.\n\nWhen used as a target, Thurisaz can affect supernatural creatures as a kind of Vim magic, these most commonly being infernal beings. It can also target thorny bushes and brambles as part of Herbam, or anything wooden that pierces or cuts.\n\nThurisaz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of the effect on Personality rolls tied to negative passions like lust or wrath.\nGeneral: The target's Might Score is reduced by (the level of this effect – 10).\nLevel 15: Cause thorny brambles to grow in an area about ten paces across.\nLevel 15: Destroy plants in an area ten paces across.\nLevel 20: Transform a living target into another living thing of approximately the same size.\nLevel 20: Transform a nonliving target into another nonliving thing of approximately the same size.\nLevel 30: Transform a living target into a nonliving thing of approximately the same size.\nLevel 30: Transform a nonliving target into a living thing of approximately the same size."
        }

        #tuGtEm4AYIO2sjXI2jRZhOWi ^"Uruz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "U" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Auroch" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "endurance, the wild"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Freya’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "This rune represents the aurochs, a large and powerful breed of cattle that roams the wilderness of Scandinavia. Julius Caesar described them as slightly smaller than the elephant and the same color and shape as a bull. They are extraordinarily strong, fast, and ferocious. Successfully hunting an aurochs makes a boy into a man, and the best way to do this is with a pit trap. Proof of the adventure is the display of the massive beast's horns, which are often bound at the tips with silver for use as drinking cups.\n\nUruz is thus a symbol of strength and stamina, as well as manhood and masculinity. There is also a parallel implied in its defense against the hunter and a man defending his home, and in the great achievement of the hunter in besting the powerful beast. When used as a target, Uruz affects the form of Animal, specifically wild or magical animals. Because of its connection to the wilderness, Uruz is also associated with rain and wild weather, occasionally translated as \"drizzle,\" and so may also be part of Auram.\n\nUruz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect on natural Ability rolls that involve Strength (but not Damage).\nGeneral: The target's Encumbrance is increased or decreased by the magnitude of this effect.\nGeneral: The target is immune to effects that target the mind that are less than this effect's level.\nLevel 30: Increase or decrease a target's Strength by one point, to no more than the average score for a being of that type. Each additional magnitude increases the number of points or the upper limit, but never more than 5 above or below the average score.\nLevel 30: Summon a wild animal that is up to Size –4.\nLevel 35: Summon a wild animal that is up to Size –1.\nLevel 40: Summon a wild animal that is up to Size +2.\nLevel 45: Summon a wild animal that is up to Size +5.\nLevel 50: Summon a wild animal that is up to Size +8."
        }

        #tAeQQ8580jeVl2rSHMArsrPW ^"Wunjo" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "W" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Joy" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "emotion, intoxication"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Freya’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "This rune means comfort, bliss, and joy. This may be a sort of intoxication, or simply the absence of suffering, and it also has connotations of glory and success in battle. Those who work together towards a common goal also fall under Wunjo's influence. Wunjo is associated with Mentem, targeting the emotions of people and intelligent beings only.\n\nWunjo Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of the effect on all natural Ability rolls involving Presence, such as telling a story, charming a companion, or leading a group.\nGeneral: Reduce the target's Fatigue or Wound Penalties by (the magnitude of this effect x 3).\nLevel 20: Cause the target to feel a powerful emotion.\nLevel 30: The target can ignore all Fatigue or Wound Penalties.\nLevel 30: Increase or decrease a target's Presence by 1 point, to no more than the average score for a being of that type. Each additional magnitude increases the number of points or the upper limit, but never more than 5 above or below the average score."
        }

        #t14g4QMBbM45qGbxJJI1fsvx ^"Ihwaz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "Y" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Yew" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "patience, the dead"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Heimdall’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "Ihwaz refers to the yew tree, the wood of which is used to make longbows and which also has associations with death and witchcraft because of a traditional practice of planting it in graveyards. When used as a target, it may affect any sort of tree or bow and should be treated as an Herbam effect. The rune may also be used to target the spirits of the dead as a Mentem effect, or a gravesite as Terram.\n\nIhwaz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target receives a bonus or penalty equal to the magnitude of this effect to natural Ability rolls associated with Intelligence, such as remembering lore or outwitting an opponent.\nGeneral: The target can sense the presence of supernatural beings with Might Score less than or equal to the level of this effect.\nGeneral: Summon a supernatural being with Might Score less than or equal to (the level of this effect – 10).\nLevel 15: The target gains the ability to sense the properties of plants within about ten paces.\nLevel 20: The target can sense dead bodies within about ten paces.\nLevel 25: Animate a corpse or carcass, as long as it is not protected by consecrated ground.\nLevel 30: Increase or decrease a target's Intelligence by 1 point, to no more than the average score for a being of that type. Each additional magnitude increases the number of points or the upper limit, but never more than 5 above or below the average score.\nLevel 35: The target can speak with the dead, so long as he is within ten paces of the corpse or grave, and it is not protected by consecrated ground.\nLevel 35: Summon a corpse or carcass, as long as it is not protected by consecrated ground.\nLevel 35: Summon a tree."
        }

        #t0okRG9skIM66U2RYnC5P398 ^"Algiz" DEF {
            EXTENDS ^"Rune"
            PROPERTIES {
                ^"Letter" STRING "Z" FIXED
                ^"Meaning" STRING "Elk" FIXED
                ^"Effects" STRING "protection, the hunt"
                ^"Aett" STRING "Heimdall’s Aett" FIXED
                ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
            }
            DESCRIPTION "This rune has many meanings, all of which mean some sort of protection. It is sometimes associated with the elk — which is said to sleep leaning against a tree so that it may more easily elude hunters — and with its antlers. The rune itself is often seen as a hand warding off a blow, and the word alu is often used in spells to mean \"protect me,\" perhaps referring to this rune. Another interpretation is as a kind of sedge-grass that grows in marshlands, which is so prickly that it cannot be grasped. In any case, this rune is most often used for the purposes of protecting a target.\n\nAlgiz almost never refers to a target directly, though because of its symbolism it can be used to affect elk, a hand, or grass, and is thus associated with Animal, Corpus, or Herbam as appropriate.\n\nAlgiz Guidelines\nGeneral: The target's Soak is increased or decreased by the effect's magnitude.\nGeneral: All supernatural targets with Might less than or equal to the level of this effect that are associated with the spell's secondary rune are warded away from the target.\nLevel 10: All things that are appropriate to the secondary rune used in this spell are warded away from the target."
        }

